('127.889.d.18.E',4,'A turbine fuel control automatically adjusts fuel flow based on:','["tire wear", "power lever setting, rpm and air conditions", "paint", "seat weight"]'::jsonb,1,'Fuel control inputs.','original'),
('127.889.d.18.F',3,'A mechanic opens the manual to the checklist for engine fuel system inspections at each service interval. She is:','["guessing", "painting lines", "locating and explaining inspection requirements for an engine fuel system", "ignoring the manual"]'::jsonb,2,'Inspection reqs.','original'),
('127.889.d.18.F',4,'A fuel system inspection looks for:','["paint chips", "seat cracks", "tire wear", "leaks, chafing, loose fittings and clogged filters"]'::jsonb,3,'Inspect for leaks.','original'),
('127.889.d.18.G',3,'A student describes how fuel moves from the tank to the cylinders when the engine runs. She is:','["explaining fuel system operation", "describing tires", "ignoring fuel", "describing seats"]'::jsonb,0,'Fuel operation.','original'),
('127.889.d.18.G',4,'An engine-driven fuel pump usually supplies fuel:','["only at idle", "at a higher pressure than the boost pump", "with no flow", "at zero pressure"]'::jsonb,1,'Pump pressure.','original'),
('127.889.d.18.H',3,'A student reads that a wrong adjustment of a turbine fuel control can cause an overtemp or overspeed. She is researching:','["tire brands", "paint choices", "the risks of adjusting turbine engine fuel controls", "no risks"]'::jsonb,2,'Turbine FCU risk.','original'),
('127.889.d.18.H',4,'Adjusting a turbine fuel control without the manual''s limits could cause:','["better economy", "less wear", "a cooler engine", "an overtemperature or overspeed"]'::jsonb,3,'Overtemp.','original'),
('127.889.d.18.I',3,'A student reads that setting a piston engine''s mixture too lean can damage the cylinders. She is researching:','["the risks of adjusting reciprocating engine fuel controls", "tire brands", "paint choices", "no risks"]'::jsonb,0,'Piston FCU risk.','original'),
