('127.889.d.22.A',3,'A student labels the cowling, baffles, fins and flaps on an air-cooled engine diagram. She is:','["identifying the components and explaining the operational theory of air cooling systems", "labeling tires", "labeling seats", "labeling lights"]'::jsonb,0,'Air cooling.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.A',4,'An air-cooled engine sheds heat mainly through:','["radiators", "cooling fins as air flows past them", "oil sumps", "fuel lines"]'::jsonb,1,'Fins and air.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.B',3,'A student explains how air enters a turbine engine nacelle, cools the case and exits. She is:','["avoiding airflow", "describing tires", "explaining the purpose and theory of turbine engine cowling air flow and turbine engine cooling", "describing seats"]'::jsonb,2,'Nacelle flow.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.B',4,'Cooling air in a turbine nacelle protects the:','["seats", "tires", "cabin only", "engine case and accessories from high heat"]'::jsonb,3,'Why cool.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.C',3,'A student studies the baffles and seals that keep hot and cool air in a turbine engine nacelle apart. She is:','["identifying the components and purpose of turbine engine baffles and methods of sealing", "describing seats", "describing tires", "avoiding baffles"]'::jsonb,0,'Turbine baffles.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.C',4,'A turbine nacelle baffle seal that is damaged can:','["cool more", "let hot air reach parts that need cooling", "cut noise", "seal perfectly"]'::jsonb,1,'Baffle damage.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.D',3,'A student learns why blankets and shrouds wrap hot engine sections to protect the airframe and fluid lines. She is:','["describing seats", "describing tires", "identifying and explaining the purpose of turbine engine insulation blankets and shrouds", "avoiding blankets"]'::jsonb,2,'Blankets.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.D',4,'An insulation blanket helps protect nearby parts from:','["oil only", "rain only", "noise only", "radiated engine heat"]'::jsonb,3,'Heat shield.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.E',3,'A student reads that bleed air from the compressor is hot and under high pressure. She is researching:','["the risks of maintenance on compressor bleed air systems", "tire brands", "paint choices", "no risks"]'::jsonb,0,'Bleed risk.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.E',4,'Before working on a bleed air duct, a technician should:','["leave it running", "shut down the engine and let the duct cool", "ignore the pressure", "touch it hot"]'::jsonb,1,'Bleed cool.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.F',3,'A student reads that running an engine right after maintenance can expose loose parts or leaks. She is researching:','["paint choices", "no risks", "the risks of ground operation of aircraft engines following maintenance", "tire brands"]'::jsonb,2,'Post-maintenance run.','original'),
('127.889.d.22.F',4,'Before a post-maintenance engine run, a technician should check that:','["chocks are off", "tools are on the engine", "fittings are loose", "tools are cleared and fittings are secure"]'::jsonb,3,'Pre-run check.','original')
